  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nSurface high pressure will build into the region today, however\nwith an upper level trough still overhead, diurnal showers will\nbe possible this afternoon. Tonight will be mostly clear and\ncool with some valley fog. Overnight low temperatures will drop\ninto the 40s. \n\nHigh temperatures today and Saturday will be mainly in the mid \nand upper 70s. Sunday is expected to trend warmer as the flow \nbecomes more westerly with highs in the upper 70s and lower 80s.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA zonal flow pattern sets up next week with several weak waves\npushing across the region. A surface frontal boundary \ndips south out of Canada on Monday and may stall out across New\nYork. This could lead to multiple rounds of showers and \nthunderstorms through the middle of next week and several\nshortwaves push through the zonal flow pattern. High \ntemperatures early next week will mainly in the upper 70s and \nlow 80s.",
